### **Identified Risks for Each Risk Class**

#### **Risk 1:**
**Description:**
The **red traffic cones** are placed in the middle of the road, **partially obscuring the ego vehicle’s view** of the road ahead. This could lead to **missed detection of pedestrians, cyclists, or other vehicles**, increasing the risk of collision.
**Severity Score:** **0.85** (High)

#### **Risk 2:**
**Description:**
The **low visibility due to rain and darkness** combined with **insufficient street lighting** may impair the ego vehicle’s **sensor performance** (cameras, LiDAR, radar), leading to **false detections or missed objects**.
**Severity Score:** **0.75** (High)

#### **Risk 3:**
**Description:**
The **speed limit sign (20 mph)** suggests a **pedestrian-heavy or sensitive area**, but the **ego vehicle may not be traveling at an appropriate speed** due to **reduced perception** from rain and cones.
**Severity Score:** **0.70** (High)

#### **Risk 4:**
**Description:**
The **white van on the right side** could **suddenly move** or **block the ego vehicle’s path**, especially if the ego vehicle misjudges its position due to **occlusions from cones or rain**.
**Severity Score:** **0.65** (Moderate-High)

#### **Risk 5:**
**Description:**
The **wet road conditions** increase the risk of **hydroplaning or reduced braking efficiency**, making it harder for the ego vehicle to **stop quickly** if an obstacle appears.
**Severity Score:** **0.60** (Moderate)

